Description: Do not run sudo setup from the read-only Nix store
 PsychLinuxConfiguration copies files into /etc with sudo. On NixOS the
 programs.psychtoolbox module does this, so the function only prints a hint.
 AssertOpenGL tries to sudo ln -s a libdc1394 soname into /lib, which is
 meaningless on Nix because Screen links its own libdc1394.
Forwarded: not-needed
---
Only in a: PsychSourceGL
--- a/Psychtoolbox/PsychLinuxConfiguration.m
+++ b/Psychtoolbox/PsychLinuxConfiguration.m
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 function usedAnswers = PsychLinuxConfiguration(answers, dontshowad)
 % PsychLinuxConfiguration([answers]) -- Optimize setup of Linux system.
 %
+% Nix: this function does nothing. Psychtoolbox lives in the read-only
+% Nix store, and the system setup below is done declaratively by the NixOS
+% option programs.psychtoolbox.enable.
+%
 % This script modifies system settings and configuration files
 % to optimize a Linux system for use with Psychtoolbox.
 %
@@ -82,6 +86,13 @@
 %                  FeralInteractive gamemode package, to switch supported gpu's into
 %                  high-performance mode for Priority() > 0, and do possible other PTB
 %                  specific optimizations beyond the default optims of the gamemode package.
+
+% Nix: skip the sudo based setup. See the help text.
+usedAnswers = '';
+fprintf('PsychLinuxConfiguration: Not needed. On NixOS, set programs.psychtoolbox.enable = true;\n');
+fprintf('PsychLinuxConfiguration: It installs the udev rules, realtime limits and the psychtoolbox group.\n');
+return;
+
 rerun = 0;
 updateinitramfs = 0;
 
